{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791128511,"nonce":"SZBg9yFaBEP9pUlazqLTUDatOr4=","message":"The ashui session, Blinc's main downstream consumer, sets word-spacing nowhere: no CSS property, no PropertyId write, nothing in its blinc_abi binding. So neither resolution would change its boxes, and it has no preference.\n\nThat removes the compatibility constraint from this decision. The choice is now purely about which behaviour Blinc wants: implement word-spacing in blinc_text's layout so the modifier does what it says, which widens any existing in-repo text that sets it, or drop it from the measurers so boxes are correct immediately and leave the modifier inert until someone implements it.","files":null}]}